at yes this maybe was a kind of  diplomatic overture to olaf schultz  yesterday a sign of kind of friendship  for his visit in moscow but no really  wide-ranging end to this crisis  right and tell us about this this day of  unity that's been declared for today  well it's an extra holiday albeit one  where ukrainians are still expected to  work it was only dreamt up by voldemort  zolensky ukraine's president a couple of  days ago so most people haven't really  had a chance to react yes behind me um  of course you can't see it because it's  too big there's a huge huge huge  flagpole with an even bigger ukrainian  flag that has just been hoisted in the  presence of some officials school  children are being encouraged to come to  class wearing national costume um  him has  the national anthem has been sung in  various places but i don't think it  really goes anywhere near national the  national holiday that ukraine has in the  summer this is just an attempt by the  government here to try and uh take the  initiative to kind of change the agenda  and to give people a sense that they're  on top of this because obviously the  biggest fear here in ukraine is that all  this talk of invasion is going to cause  panic we've already seen the exchange  rate weakened we've seen people buying  supplies of food in case  some kind of conflict were to happen and  that is what ukraine's government now is  worried about in the short term is panic  among the population we've seen cyber  attacks coming from russia yesterday on  government ministries and on banks  so it's not as if this pressure is  somehow subsiding russia's basically  blockading ukraine's ports on the black  sea its exports through exercise in the  black sea so yes some limited signs of  de-escalation but a very nervy ukrainian  government here trying to convince its  population that it's on top of things  that it has support from its western  partners and that there is no reason to  panic in the immediate short term all 